       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. 9,000 mg/day of acetaminophen has no recognized indication. It is more than twice the maximum daily dose, and it risks acute liver injury and liver failure even in a patient with normal liver function. I can't see a clinical scenario where it would be safe, and I can't reliably prevent harm once the order is active.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a standard regimen right away.** For example, 1,000 mg PO three times daily (3,000 mg/day), or 1,000 mg PO four times daily (4,000 mg/day) if you want the maximum.\n- **Help you with a different goal.** If you need stronger analgesia or antipyresis than acetaminophen gives, I can enter an adjunct or alternative agent.\n- **Check for a typo.** If the intended total was 3,000 mg/day, tell me and I'll enter it that way.\n\nIf you still think a non-standard dose is justified, such as a protocolized toxicology or research regimen, that should go through pharmacy and your institution's override process. Tell me which of these you'd like."
      }
